    "solution": "Let A, B be the events of choosing each bag, and R the event the ball is red. P(A) = P(B) = 1/2. P(R|A) = 3/5, P(R|B) = 2/6 = 1/3. By Bayes theorem: P(A|R) = P(A)P(R|A) / [P(A)P(R|A) + P(B)P(R|B)] = (0.5 x 0.6) / (0.5 x 0.6 + 0.5 x 0.3333) = 0.3 / 0.46667 = 0.6429. Write out the partition (Bag A / Bag B) as a small table before applying the formula; it prevents mixing up P(R|A) with P(A|R).",
